  "description": {
    "text": "The prize cards of BattleZone, the organized play Wizards of the Coast ran from November 2002 in its last year with the Pokémon license. Stores ran it as a weekly league or a monthly tournament, with a prize kit for each season: 16 Classic promos, eight Best of Game cards with a gold foil Winner stamp, and one jumbo Winner card, which is not holo and has its stamp printed. In a tournament the stamped cards went to the top four players and the head judge; in a league the season's best players each got one, and the top one to four players the jumbo. Each season had a Best of Game card of its own, and its unstamped copy came back a few months later as a later season's Classic promo.\n\nWizards lost the license before the June and July 2003 seasons were played. Their tournament kits had gone out, but not their league kits, so Rocket's Mewtwo and Rocket's Hitmonchan exist only with the Winner stamp and as jumbos. Professor Elm, given out at Gen Con 2003, has no Winner or jumbo version. Electabuzz, Hitmonchan, Professor Elm, Rocket's Mewtwo and Rocket's Hitmonchan are reverse holo; Rocket's Scizor, Rocket's Sneasel, Dark Ivysaur and Dark Venusaur are not."
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A \"BEST\" logo, and a number out of 9"
  },
